  "body": "What happens: the `linux` job of `release.yml` run 43644441134 (tag `v0.20.0`) fails in the step \"Assemble Linux packages\". The release `v0.20.0` has no Linux assets. The jobs `aur`, `snap` and `flatpak` did not run.\n\nEvidence:\n```\nerror: Installed (but unpackaged) file(s) found:\n   /usr/share/icons/hicolor/128x128/apps/camcraft.png\n   /usr/share/icons/hicolor/16x16/apps/camcraft.png\n   /usr/share/icons/hicolor/256x256/apps/camcraft.png\n   /usr/share/icons/hicolor/32x32/apps/camcraft.png\n   /usr/share/icons/hicolor/48x48/apps/camcraft.png\nRPM build errors:\n```\n\nCause (not confirmed): the RPM spec installs the hicolor icons but its `%files` section does not list them.\n\nThe Windows, macOS and FreeBSD assets and the documentation site are published. The tag does not move.\n\nDone means: the RPM spec lists the icon files, a local or dispatched packaging run builds the RPM, and the Linux assets are attached to release `v0.20.0` or the next release.\n",
